  "summary": "Bundled skill scripts with routine network calls",
  "details": "Package ships a collection of skill bundles under bundled-skills/. Static keyword matches surface in utility scripts whose purpose is ordinary: base_scraper.py and serve_api.py perform HTTP GET/POST for a scraping/API skill; rclone-cli/scripts/install.sh runs curl against rclone.org (the rclone project's official domain) as part of an rclone installer; youtube-notetaker/scripts/verify.sh performs curl GET requests for a verification helper; run-benchmarks.sh contains benchmark setup code. None of the matched locations show reads of installer credential paths (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc), environment scraping, hardcoded attacker C2, obfuscated destinations, or install-time lifecycle hooks fetching and executing attacker-controlled code. The matches are keyword co-occurrence (curl/ping/GET/POST/install) in scripts whose documented purpose is to perform HTTP operations for their respective skills.",
